
# PLP Python Week 4 - Functions

- `welcome.py`: Uses one function to greet three people.
- `toolbox.py`: Contains functions to double numbers, check passing scores, and greet people.
- `README.md`: Describes the assignment files and what I learned.

The hardest function to write was `greet` because it uses an optional parameter with a default value. I learned that Python uses "Hello" when no other greeting is provided.

